WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:02.103
- I think this is the
only job I haven't quit.

00:00:02.103 --> 00:00:05.060
(light jazzy music)

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.318
- My first job was working at a toy store,

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:10.985
and I was 16 and I was
really, really skinny.

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:12.840
They would have these events where they'd

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.750
rent this Hello Kitty costume

00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:16.996
and I was the only person
who could fit in it.

00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:19.168
- My first job was when I was 15 years old

00:00:19.168 --> 00:00:21.371
at the Cleveland Metroparks Zoo.

00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:22.476
My job was to walk around the

00:00:22.476 --> 00:00:24.913
Roaring Lion Cafe picking up trash,

00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:26.884
and I pulled out a bag

00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:30.854
and I looked down and
there was a mother yelling

00:00:30.854 --> 00:00:33.359
and there was like a milky white liquid

00:00:33.359 --> 00:00:35.141
pouring on her baby's head.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.546
- My first job was an
employee at Hot Dog on a Stick

00:00:38.546 --> 00:00:41.732
and you have to wear these
terrible, terrible outfits.

00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:44.845
Every time you made new
batter for the corn dogs

00:00:44.845 --> 00:00:46.513
you would like, whisk it
up, and then you would

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:50.465
have to yell to the whole
entire food court "Batter Up!".

00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:52.194
- I was in a lot of character costumes,

00:00:52.194 --> 00:00:55.572
I did Hello Kitty, this giant
teddy bear called Muffy,

00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:58.764
a Groovy Girl, and I was also
Curious George in a parade.

00:00:58.764 --> 00:01:02.118
And Curious George was really
hard because it was so hot.

00:01:02.224 --> 00:01:05.843
- My worst job was at a
clothing retail store.

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:09.193
We had to fold with precision
and people would come in

00:01:09.193 --> 00:01:11.298
and immediately mess up the fold.

00:01:11.298 --> 00:01:11.893
Sometimes people would be like

00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:13.028
"Do you think this looks good?"

00:01:13.028 --> 00:01:14.466
and it's like "Do you think it looks good?

00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:15.663
"I don't know, where you goin'?"

00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:18.213
- The worst job I ever
had was what is considered

00:01:18.213 --> 00:01:20.175
categorically the worst job in America,

00:01:20.175 --> 00:01:23.458
which is a file clerk in a hospital.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:26.937
- I, like, was fired and
quit at the same time,

00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:28.965
but mainly because I told
this lady I was gonna quit

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:30.794
and then she told me I was fired anyway.

00:01:30.935 --> 00:01:34.239
- I quit Friendlys, I quit
American Eagle, I quit,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.319
I mean, I don't even have enough fingers.

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:38.352
- Tons of horrible day work in factories.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:40.002
Look at this, this guy can't work in a,

00:01:40.002 --> 00:01:41.948
I can't work in a factory,
what are you talkin' about?

00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:43.013
- Sometimes you gotta get fired,

00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:44.727
cuz you got to get the hell out of there.

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:47.311
- I made up a lie that
it was a family emergency

00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:49.938
and left a week before I was supposed to

00:01:49.938 --> 00:01:52.136
cuz I just couldn't handle it any more.

00:01:52.136 --> 00:01:54.092
I even fake cried.

00:01:54.384 --> 00:01:55.588
- I've learned to be a good worker

00:01:56.202 --> 00:01:58.073
from my working career,
no matter where I worked

00:01:58.073 --> 00:01:59.424
I was good at my job.

00:01:59.424 --> 00:02:00.594
- If you're going to have a shitty job,

00:02:00.855 --> 00:02:03.943
do it with a friend of yours
so you can be shitty together.

00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:06.776
- Be careful when you
sit on Hello Kitty's lap.

00:02:06.914 --> 00:02:09.105
Also just don't get too
handsy with Hello Kitty,

00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:10.354
you don't know who's inside.

00:02:10.354 --> 00:02:11.999
Or for any mascot for that matter.

00:02:11.999 --> 00:02:13.744
Keep like a five foot distance.

